00:00:00,187 --> 00:00:02,000
Four ways to buy gold on MCX.

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:05,312
Same gold. Which price is fair?

3
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:07,375
Per gram of pure gold, they almost match.

4
00:00:07,562 --> 00:00:09,317
Meet Parity: MCX gold futures intelligence. A guided tour in 8 short stops.

5
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:15,683
This is Parity. Each page answers one question about MCX gold futures.

6
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:19,017
Dotted words explain themselves. Just hover.

7
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:22,850
Every page starts with the answer: the In short box.

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,583
Latest closes, all four in ₹ per gram of pure gold.

9
00:00:26,633 --> 00:00:30,917
Premium: how much dearer than GOLDM. Usual: its normal level.

10
00:00:30,967 --> 00:00:35,017
All near their usual level today, so the signal is quiet.

11
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:38,083
Lost? Ctrl + K searches the whole site.

12
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:44,917
The brief asked for five things. Each card: the ask, what we built, the proof.

13
00:00:44,967 --> 00:00:49,083
All five done. Every line of the final challenge answered.

14
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:54,617
Contracts compared two at a time, per gram of pure gold.

15
00:00:54,667 --> 00:00:58,317
GOLDM vs GOLDTEN hugs zero: same gold, same price.

16
00:00:58,367 --> 00:01:02,517
The 8 g coin is always dearer: about 60 bp (0.6%) per gram.

17
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:06,783
In the Dec 2025 – Mar 2026 crash that gap blew out past 2.6%.

18
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:11,350
Dearer in all 41 contract months: a lasting premium, not a mistake.

19
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:16,883
Each dot is one contract. Further right = expires later.

20
00:01:16,933 --> 00:01:20,883
Later costs more, like rent on gold: the cost of carry.

21
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:24,817
90 days ago the line sat elsewhere: gold itself moved.

22
00:01:24,867 --> 00:01:29,217
Time moves GOLDM only about 0.6% a month. Gold moves far more.

23
00:01:30,767 --> 00:01:34,750
Buy the cheap one, sell the dear one. Do you make money?

24
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:38,517
Slippage is lost on every fill. With perfect fills…

25
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:42,083
…profit looks big. At 10 bp most of it vanishes.

26
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:46,050
So every result is shown at 5 bp, the realistic middle.

27
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:50,750
Strategy A's profit came almost all from one crash month: Jan 2026.

28
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:55,750
Strategy B, the fair-price rule: fewer trades, steadier, still positive.

29
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:00,383
Most backtests skip costs and test on the data they were tuned on…

30
00:02:00,433 --> 00:02:03,583
…so the numbers look huge. Not real money.

31
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:07,350
Ours: real costs, on data the rules had never seen.

32
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:12,783
The hardest exam: 8 sealed years (2016–2023), opened only after the rules froze.

33
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:17,917
Strategy A failed. Strategy B made money in both windows: small, but real.

34
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:22,883
A bet on gold rising? No. Every trade's profit splits into gap and gold.

35
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:28,783
Is any contract far from fair price now? Black marker = today.

36
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:32,883
Past the red ticks, an alert fires. Today all are normal.

37
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:38,117
66 alerts since 2023. Typically the gap closed 51 bp within 10 trading days.

38
00:02:38,167 --> 00:02:43,150
Each alert logs what happened next. Most days the honest answer is: wait.

39
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,583
Each bar is one contract, first trading day to expiry.

40
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:53,150
Each dash is a trade: green won, red lost. Pink = the 2026 crash.

41
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:58,250
The dark end is the run-up to delivery. Strategy B always exits before it.

42
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:04,450
Built on 723 official MCX files: 12,021 rows, 0 unexplained errors.

43
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:08,783
Rules like the delivery period come from MCX's own documents.

44
00:03:08,833 --> 00:03:11,383
And for late nights: dark mode.

45
00:03:11,654 --> 00:03:15,842
What you just saw: a fair comparison, the curve explained, honest backtests, 8 sealed years, quiet alerts, and the contract calendar.

46
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:18,342
The honest answer: a small, real edge. Tested honestly, doubts included.

47
